{
  "text": "For every pair of real numbers k and h, if k ≥ 2 and 0 < h < 1/4, then both k/2 ≤ k(k+h+1)/(2k+h) and k(k+h+1)/(2k+h) ≤ (4/5)k hold for that same pair. All operations and inequalities are over the real numbers. The numerical constants 2, 1/4, 1/2, and 4/5 are fixed and independent of k and h; there are no additional parameters or existentially chosen constants. Division is totalized real division, with division by zero equal to zero, but the hypotheses ensure 2k+h > 0, so the displayed quotient has a nonzero denominator.",
